      {
        "thread_id": "TH2",
        "thread_goal": "Define processes, compliance requirements, and documentation standards.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M20",
            "speaker_id": 200052,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hi team, I am starting on T3 for compliance. We need to think about the documents we need from farmers for our services. What should we ask them to bring?",
            "mentions": [
              88246,
              83675,
              59001
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M21",
            "speaker_id": 88246,
            "reply_to": "M20",
            "text": "Thanks for kicking this off. A good way to structure this would be to define the minimum required documents per service. For 'Financial Intake', I'd suggest we need their national ID and proof of land ownership. For 'Admin Support', it would depend on the form.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M22",
            "speaker_id": 83675,
            "reply_to": "M21",
            "text": "In my previous roles, we often needed certified copies. Is that required here? It can be a hassle for clients.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M23",
            "speaker_id": 200052,
            "reply_to": "M22",
            "text": "Certified copies? I am not sure what the specific regulations are for this. I would have to check.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M24",
            "speaker_id": 88246,
            "reply_to": "M23",
            "text": "Let's prioritize accessibility for the pilot. I propose for D3 that our minimum documentation set is: 1) National ID (we take a photocopy), 2) Land Title/Lease (photocopy), and 3) our signed intake form. We can verify the originals on site. This can be documented in A5. How does that sound?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D3"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M25",
            "speaker_id": 59001,
            "reply_to": "M24",
            "text": "We need to be very clear in our communications that they must bring these papers. Some might forget.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "bulb",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M26",
            "speaker_id": 88246,
            "reply_to": "M25",
            "text": "Good point. @59001, please ensure that's highlighted in the A3 onboarding guidelines.",
            "mentions": [
              59001
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M27",
            "speaker_id": 200052,
            "reply_to": "M24",
            "text": "Ok, ID, land title, and our form. That is simple enough. I agree for D3.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D3"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M28",
            "speaker_id": 83675,
            "reply_to": "M24",
            "text": "Yes, that's a practical solution.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M29",
            "speaker_id": 88246,
            "reply_to": "M28",
            "text": "Great, D3 is settled. Now for the standard intake form for T6. To avoid repeat questions, we should have one form that covers all services. I suggest sections for: Personal Details, Farm Details (size, crops/livestock), and a checklist for Service Requested. This data will feed into our tracking sheet, A4.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T6",
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D4"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M30",
            "speaker_id": 200052,
            "reply_to": "M29",
            "text": "We must include a data privacy statement on the form. I can find some standard wording for that.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M31",
            "speaker_id": 59001,
            "reply_to": "M29",
            "text": "We should ask what crops they are growing.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M32",
            "speaker_id": 83675,
            "reply_to": "M29",
            "text": "And if they have other loans. That's important for financial services.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M33",
            "speaker_id": 88246,
            "reply_to": "M32",
            "text": "All good inputs. Let's finalize the form fields for D4: Personal Info (with privacy clause), Farm Profile, Financial Profile, and Service Requested. For data storage, all digital records will be in a secure folder, with physical copies in a locked cabinet. Agreed?",
            "mentions": [],
